diff --git a/integrations/required-agents/qualification/README.md b/integrations/required-agents/qualification/README.md
index 6fb98cbd0..7869adfde 100644
--- a/integrations/required-agents/qualification/README.md
+++ b/integrations/required-agents/qualification/README.md
@@ -109,3 +109,63 @@ they do not carry structured admission-state metadata. Consumers must preserve
 the original unknown outcome. An unsigned duplicate rejection also does not
 establish no original effect. Successful replay after restart returns the
 original signed receipt and preserves the observer's sentinel.
+## Dedicated native qualification environment
+
+Keep qualification separate from shared application services. The selected
+source `de84fc306efbb4c8dd6de748d0ad2a8d695fd30e` accepts only native x86_64
+enforcement. An aarch64 Docker guest can build artifacts and inspect recovery
+copies, but it cannot qualify that enforcing runtime.
+
+On the inspected Colima 0.8.4 and Lima 2.1.4 installation:
+
+```sh
+colima start chio-native-qualification-x86 \
+  --runtime docker --vm-type qemu --arch x86_64 \
+  --cpus 4 --memory 8 --disk 40 --activate=false --template=false
+colima --profile chio-native-qualification-x86 ssh -- uname -m
+docker --context colima-chio-native-qualification-x86 info
+```
+
+Every host Docker command must select its context. Inside the Linux resource
+owner, select the guest's own context explicitly. The owner launcher pins the
+resolved endpoint and daemon identity and checks them again before restart.
+Its private stores and credentials belong in the Linux owner environment, away
+from the agent host. Never copy private operator records into public evidence.
+
+The [cross-build recipe](./Dockerfile.kernel-cross) compiles pinned-source Linux
+x86_64 artifacts on a native ARM builder. It pins Rust 1.94.1 and retains the
+dependency lock, toolchain metadata, distribution package inventory and binary
+hashes. Build it from a clean selected checkout using an explicit ARM Docker
+context. The recipe selects `docker-release` with optimization level 1, LTO off
+and overflow checks enabled. Its profile and artifact identity must be retained.
+Package versions are inventoried rather than frozen, so a new
+build needs independent identity and qualification.
+
+Infrastructure availability is an admission prerequisite. Passing shell,
+storage, inode and image reads does not prove live approval, resource custody,
+original-outcome recovery or release qualification. The enforcing runtime also
+needs an independently qualified launch contract: an ordinary Docker CLI needs
+socket creation that the selected native cage forbids. A weaker migration stage
+cannot satisfy an enforcing-profile gate. Preserve failed state and the exact
+diagnostic before revising that contract.
+
+The selected filesystem server's actual fourteen-tool inventory includes MCP
+`execution: {taskSupport: "forbidden"}` metadata. The selected manifest
+provisioner rejects that metadata. A reviewed synchronous four-tool projection
+was used only to probe enforcing launch; it does not qualify the full inventory
+or its metadata binding. Retain the actual discovery response and qualify the
+publisher manifest contract before claiming resource acceptance.
+
+The [reference-tool cross-build](./Dockerfile.reference-tools-cross) supplies a
+separate static, single-threaded file-writer experiment. This is a different
+resource profile and cannot qualify the Docker filesystem server. Its
+`write_file` implementation calls `sync_all` after writing a precreated exact
+file. On the selected enforcing build, the writer was killed by seccomp at
+x86_64 syscall 74 (`fsync`) after one independently observed write. The kernel
+retained `outcome_unknown_after_dispatch`; restart did not redispatch it.
+No verified original result was returned, so this does not satisfy original
+outcome recovery. A file's observed contents also do not prove that a failed
+durability barrier committed them to stable storage. Qualify a reviewed
+durability contract or resource-owned broker before retrying that acceptance
+case with fresh disposable state. Do not remove the durability barrier or
+weaken the cage to turn this failure into a passing check.
diff --git a/integrations/required-agents/qualification/test_owner_docker_context.py b/integrations/required-agents/qualification/test_owner_docker_context.py
